.TH H96-KERNEL-SWITCH 8 "2026-10-23" "h96-kernel-switch" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
h96-kernel-switch \- boot staged kernel as guarded trial, confirm or roll back
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B h96-kernel-switch
.B list
|
.B status
|
.B default
|
.B dtb
.br
.B h96-kernel-switch try
.I KREL
.RB [ \-\-auto\-confirm ]
.RB [ \-\-keep\-dtb ]
.br
.B h96-kernel-switch
.B confirm
|
.B rollback
.RB [ \-\-keep\-dtb ]
|
.B dtb-plain
.br
.B h96-kernel-switch
.B prune
|
.B in-use
.I KREL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kernel packages stage files under /usr/lib/h96-kernel/KREL and never write /boot.
Vendor U-Boot on H96 MAX V58 has no try-once slot; boot.scr loads /boot/Image,
/boot/uInitrd and /boot/dtb/FDTFILE.
.B h96-kernel-switch
copies one staged kernel into generation directory /boot/h96ks/KREL.gN
(Image, uInitrd, fdt). Image and uInitrd link through /boot/h96ks/cur, and so
does board DTB once DTB differs between kernels; one rename of h96ks/cur
switches all three, so power loss leaves either old or new set. Boot guard
runs early on next boot: on trial kernel it points h96ks/cur back to previous
generation at once, so hang, panic or watchdog reset lands on previous kernel.
Only
.B confirm
during trial boot keeps new kernel as default.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Staged kernels with flags running, default, in-boot, trial; below each, its
generations KREL.gN with roles default (h96ks/cur), trial, trial-previous,
rollback-target and running (banner of generation Image equals /proc/version).
.TP
.B status
Default release, link targets, generations with roles, recorded trial, last
results.
.TP
.B default
Prints release that boot files start; exit status 1 when unknown.
.TP
.BI try " KREL"
Checks staged sha256 sums, modules.dep and release string embedded in Image,
builds initramfs with mkinitramfs and mkimage outside /boot, checks free space
on /boot (new files plus 16 MiB reserve), writes new generation through hidden
temporary directory, enables guard units, records trial, then moves h96ks/cur.
First run converts plain-name Image and uInitrd links into h96ks/cur links;
every conversion step keeps content each boot name resolves to (previous
generation holds hard links to current files and DTB copy). Refuses when trial
is recorded, when KREL is running or default and staged Image and DTB equal
in-boot generation, when /boot is read-only, when
extlinux directory exists, or when Image or uInitrd is not link. Also
refuses while h96-undervolt trial is recorded, and DTB change while
h96-undervolt change is active (use
.BR \-\-keep\-dtb ).
Same release, new content: when KREL is default or running but staged Image or
DTB differs from in-boot generation,
.B try
makes new generation KREL.gN+1; boot guard tells trial boot from fallback by
Image banner (build number and date) when generations differ there, else by
boot id and h96ks/cur.
.B \-\-auto\-confirm
confirms trial 180 s after boot when multi-user.target is active.
.B \-\-keep\-dtb
leaves board DTB as is; generation carries current DTB.
.TP
.B confirm
Run during trial boot: points h96ks/cur at trial generation for good.
.TP
.B rollback
With trial recorded: cancels it. Without trial: returns h96ks/cur to
generation that was default before last confirm; running it again returns to
confirmed generation. Refuses when board DTB is plain file that differs from
DTB of target generation, since rollback switches Image and uInitrd only;
.B \-\-keep\-dtb
rolls back with current DTB.
.TP
.BI prune " KREL|GEN"
Removes generations and plain-name files of KREL from /boot unless h96ks/cur,
boot links or records name them. With generation name GEN (KREL.gN): removes
that generation only, unless h96ks/cur or records name it.
.TP
.BI in-use " KREL|GEN"
Prints roles of KREL, or of generation GEN, in boot files: default, trial,
trial-previous, rollback-target; exit status 1 when none. Kernel packages use it to skip
install hint and to refuse removal.
.TP
.B dtb
Read only. Prints path=, layout= (plain, managed, link), file= (resolved
file) and trial= (none or recorded phase) for board DTB.
.BR h96-undervolt (8)
uses it to refuse writes into generations.
.TP
.B dtb-plain
Turns managed DTB link back into plain file holding content of
h96ks/cur/fdt (temporary name, read-back, rename). Refuses while trial is
recorded. Later
.B try
links DTB again when staged DTB differs, unless
.BR \-\-keep\-dtb .
.SH FILES
.TP
/boot/h96ks/cur, /boot/h96ks/KREL.gN
Active generation link and generation directories.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/trial
Recorded trial or unfinished confirm or rollback: phase, previous and new
generation.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/last
Generations of last confirm or rollback, used by rollback.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/log, result
Action log and outcome lines.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-undervolt-trial, /var/lib/h96-undervolt-state
Read by
.BR try :
h96-undervolt trial recorded, undervolt or overclock active.
.SH LIMITS
Failure before boot guard runs (early panic, initramfs failure without reset
to userspace) repeats trial boot, since h96ks/cur still names trial generation
at that point. Recovery then needs rescue media or reflash.
U-Boot must follow relative links with directory parts (Image to
h96ks/cur/Image, h96ks/cur to generation); not yet booted on hardware.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR h96-undervolt (8),
.BR mkinitramfs (8),
.BR mkimage (1)
